shape theory.physics.su3 : theory.physics.gauge, theory.physics.su2 {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 3.5 (Internal Orientation / SU(3)).
// All three generators projected as values give SU(3)_XYZ: the
// full internal structure. The orientation of the triple {X, Y, Z}
// as a system.
//
// There is only one SU(3). It requires all three generators.
// SU(3) IS the internal face of the spatial lattice.
// The 3D spatial lattice uses {X, Y, Z} as directions;
// SU(3) uses {X, Y, Z} as values.
// Two projections of the same thing.
//
// Internally: a place where structure can go (lattice substrate).
// Externally: neutrality (orientation symmetry always maintained).
//
// No SU(4) or higher: there is no fourth generator to project.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.gauge, theory.physics.su2
  """
}
